1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,900
Longest Common Prefix — LeetCode 14

2
00:00:01,900 --> 00:00:05,400
Problem: given a list of strings, find the longest prefix they all share.

3
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:09,400
Example: flower, flow, flight all start with "fl", so the answer is "fl".

4
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:13,600
Key idea: stack the words and read straight down the columns.

5
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:18,600
If every word has the same character in a column, it's part of the prefix — keep going.

6
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:22,600
The first column where they disagree is exactly where the prefix ends.

7
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:25,600
Take column 0 of the first word — that's 'f'. Every word has 'f'. Keep it.

8
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:28,600
Column 1 is 'l', and all three match. Prefix is now "fl".

9
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:33,000
Column 2: flower and flow have 'o', but flight has 'i'. A mismatch — stop.

10
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:36,500
The prefix is everything before that column: "fl".

11
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:41,500
Bonus, cleaner code: only the lexicographic smallest and largest strings matter — compare just those two.

12
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:46,000
Vertical scan is O(S) over the total characters, O(1) extra space.

13
